@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/dispatcher#> .
@prefix courier: <http://example.org/orexis/courier#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix planning: <http://example.org/orexis/planning#> .

<> a planning:ConstraintGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  ONE CONSTRAINT, and a constraint rather than a desire: two vans cannot share a cell. That is
#  physics, not a preference — a world in which they do is not a bad world the dispatcher should
#  set about mending but a world that cannot be — so it is a `planning:Constraint`, of another
#  modality than the desires in `desires.ttl`, and the agent holds it as it holds those.
#
#  AUTHORED AS THE AVOIDED STATE, `planning:unmetWhen`, the honest polarity for a prohibition
#  (#892): one select whose rows are the vans sharing a cell, violated where it yields a row, the
#  cell projected as `?value`. The compiler would take a shape under `planning:metWhen` as readily;
#  this is the form that reads as it evaluates.
#
#  WHAT IT DOES. The search weighs it in every possible world it weighs a want in, and a world with
#  two vans on a cell is marked `planning:impossible` — off the frontier, never an achiever — which is
#  what keeps the two parcels' joint plan off the other van's cell. Its footprint, `at` on vans
#  joined on the cell, is what couples the two parcels' wants into one search, since a plan for
#  either could collide with a plan for the other (one-mind-couples-the-wants-a-constraint-can-make-collide).
#  And posed with both vans on one cell the world is REFUSED — by `orexis-onboard` before anything
#  is granted, and said in the log by every pass — never repaired: no want is minted from it, since
#  it is no desire. It was a desire, the dispatcher's aversion, and a drive parted the vans; that
#  made the world's physics something the agent wanted, which is the wrong modality
#  (knowledge/domain/planning/constraint.md).

:dispatcher planning:holds :no_cell_holds_two_vans .

:no_cell_holds_two_vans a planning:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "no cell holds two vans" ;
    planning:unmetWhen :two_vans_on_one_cell .

:two_vans_on_one_cell
    sh:message "two vans stand on one cell" ;
    sh:select """PREFIX courier: <http://example.org/orexis/courier#>
        SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
            $this a courier:Van ;
                courier:at ?value .
            ?other a courier:Van ;
                courier:at ?value .
            FILTER(?other != $this)
        }""" .
